#
# spherequads.obj - Sphere, quad faces
#
# Geometry:   a unit sphere centred on the origin, its axis along y, so it
#             spans 2 x 2 x 2. The poles are at y = -1 and y = +1.
# Components: 114 vertices, 153 UV coordinates, 114 vertex normals, and 128 faces,
#             8 rows of 16. The two rows at the poles are triangles and the
#             6 rows between them are quads. 16 meridians and 8 parallels put
#             22.5 degrees between every cut both ways, so a face is as wide as
#             it is tall and a checker laid on the rows comes out square. The
#             normals are the analytic outward normals, which on a unit sphere
#             are the vertex positions themselves. The UVs run 0 to 1, u around
#             the equator and v pole to pole, with the seam column duplicated so
#             the wrap does not fold the map back over itself.
# Used by:    boingball.
#
o spherequads
